00:09:32.080 --> 00:09:32.879
They love me, they hate me.
他们爱我，他们恨我。

00:09:32.879 --> 00:09:38.320
You're always kind of, and when you're young, you don't know not to read the comments until you learn, don't read the comments.
你总是处于这种状态，当你年轻的时候，你不知道不要去读评论，直到你学会了——别读评论。

00:09:38.320 --> 00:09:40.320
You'd still have to relearn that one sometimes, I'm 50.
有时候你还得重新学习这一点，我都50岁了。

00:09:40.320 --> 00:09:41.320
Yeah.
是啊。

00:09:41.320 --> 00:09:42.320
Yeah.
是啊。

00:09:42.320 --> 00:09:43.320
Why would Josh say that about me?
为什么乔什要那样说我？

00:09:43.320 --> 00:09:45.519
I thought we...
我以为我们……

00:09:45.519 --> 00:09:57.080
But I think that I was very rattled by the pressure of being at the center of the show, the erosion of my anonymity.
但我认为我被处于节目中心的压力，以及匿名性的丧失给震慑住了。

00:09:57.080 --> 00:10:08.639
I always joke when I did the graduate on Broadway with Kathleen Turner, I used to say I was famous for 15 minutes from 10 o'clock to 10.15 on a half block of West 45th Street.
我常开玩笑说，当我和凯瑟琳·特纳在百老汇演《毕业生》时，我常说我曾有过15分钟的成名时刻，就在西45街半个街区，从10点到10点15分。

00:10:08.639 --> 00:10:13.120
I signed autographs, took pictures, and then I rounded the corner.
我签了名，拍了照，然后转过街角。

00:10:13.120 --> 00:10:15.279
The radius was 100 feet of string.
半径只有100英尺。

00:10:15.279 --> 00:10:19.440
Yeah, and then I was, I was, I blended in with the rest of New York City.
是的，然后我就融入了纽约市的其他人群中。

00:10:19.440 --> 00:10:20.720
Yes, yeah, yeah.
是的，没错，没错。

00:10:20.720 --> 00:10:36.879
And there was just something so different about starring on a TV show on CBS on prime time, And I don't want to overstate, like, I wasn't a beetle, I wasn't, you know, I could, I still went to my coffee shop and wrote and did all that.
在哥伦比亚广播公司的黄金时段主演一部电视剧，感觉确实非常不同，我不想夸大其词，我不是披头士乐队，我不是……你知道，我仍然可以去咖啡店写作，做所有那些事。

00:10:36.879 --> 00:10:54.840
It's just, I started noticing as the years went on, more and more people were looking at me, whispering about me, you know, I got, I started to get tables real fast at restaurants, you know, airports became a place where I'd have to take a lot of photos with people.
只是，随着时间的推移，我开始注意到越来越多的人在看我，对我指指点点，你知道，我开始在餐厅很快就能订到桌子，你知道，机场成了我必须和很多人合影的地方。

00:10:54.840 --> 00:11:03.519
And it's just, you know, you think that that is like, oh, great, you're a young actor, that means you're making it, you're making your mark, people know who you are.
你以为这很棒，哦，太好了，你是个年轻演员，这意味着你成功了，你留下了自己的印记，人们知道你是谁。

00:11:03.519 --> 00:11:11.960
But for me, I found it somewhat thrilling, depending on the day and somewhat like vertigo inducing, like really, it just threw me.
但对我来说，这有时令人兴奋，取决于当天的状态，有时又让人感到眩晕，真的，它让我不知所措。

00:11:11.960 --> 00:11:14.919
I didn't know if I liked it necessarily.
我甚至不知道自己是否真的喜欢它。

00:11:14.919 --> 00:11:25.279
And, you know, I just think that fame and visibility is an infinitely more complicated thing and then it looks like from the outside.
而且，你知道，我只是觉得名气和曝光度是一件比从外面看起来要复杂得多的事情。

00:11:25.279 --> 00:11:26.360
At least it was for me.
至少对我来说是这样。

00:11:26.360 --> 00:11:35.519
And I wrote you this little ditty to sing to you in New York City.
我为你写了这首小曲子，要在纽约市唱给你听。

00:11:35.559 --> 00:11:46.309
We'll be right back.
我们马上回来。

00:11:46.309 --> 00:11:49.019
Back to the show.
回到节目。

00:11:49.019 --> 00:11:58.379
You know, the first two seasons I had never asked myself if I drank too much because I wasn't like, I wasn't a problem drinker.
你知道，前两季我从未问过自己是否喝得太多，因为我不是那种……我不是个酗酒成性的人。

00:11:58.379 --> 00:11:59.419
I wasn't a blackout drinker.
我不是那种喝到断片的人。

00:11:59.419 --> 00:12:03.139
I wasn't someone who people said, hey, you probably had a little too much last night.
我不是那种会被人说“嘿，你昨晚可能喝得有点多”的人。

00:12:03.139 --> 00:12:06.940
I don't know if you remember, Craig was a long time ago, but like I was a pretty charming drunk.
我不知道你还记不记得，克雷格，那是很久以前的事了，但我当时是个挺迷人的酒鬼。

00:12:06.940 --> 00:12:09.500
Like I would drink a lot of beers and- Oh, you were a delightful drunk.
比如我会喝很多啤酒，然后——哦，你是个令人愉快的酒鬼。

00:12:09.500 --> 00:12:10.500
You were not too drunk.
你喝得并不算太醉。

00:12:10.500 --> 00:12:11.340
You were a good amount of drunk.
你喝得恰到好处。

00:12:11.340 --> 00:12:13.860
We could huddle in the corner and compliment each other.
我们可以挤在角落里互相恭维。

00:12:13.860 --> 00:12:15.259
That was my memory of drinking with Greg Thomas.
这就是我对和格雷格·托马斯一起喝酒的记忆。

00:12:15.259 --> 00:12:16.820
We were very lovely drunks together.
我们在一起时是非常可爱的酒鬼。

00:12:16.820 --> 00:12:25.480
Yeah, and but I never really considered it, but I did notice in the second season, my drinking ticked up, you know.
是的，但我从未真正考虑过这个问题，但我确实注意到在第二季，我的饮酒量增加了，你知道。

00:12:25.480 --> 00:12:34.759
I remember I would go home and I would, I remember having like being very easily kind of killing a bottle of red wine, getting high.
我记得我会回家，我记得自己很容易就能喝掉一瓶红酒，然后变得飘飘然。

00:12:34.759 --> 00:12:39.279
And then not quite remembering, I'm waking up in my bed, but not quite remembering.
然后不太记得了，我在床上醒来，但不太记得发生了什么。

00:12:39.279 --> 00:12:40.799
Very end of the night, it's a little old.
深夜的时候，有点老套。

00:12:40.799 --> 00:12:41.960
Not quite remembering that.
不太记得了。

00:12:41.960 --> 00:12:43.840
It was sanded off, you know?
就像被磨平了一样，你知道吗？

00:12:43.840 --> 00:12:56.279
And I had a couple nights and a couple of things where I was like, I'm really drinking more out of anxiety than I had before, like enjoying that experience socially with friends or whatever.
我有几个晚上和几件事让我觉得，我喝酒更多是因为焦虑，而不是像以前那样为了和朋友社交享受那种体验。

00:12:56.279 --> 00:12:57.720
Yeah, yeah, I know what you mean.
是的，是的，我明白你的意思。

00:12:57.720 --> 00:13:04.392
So I, um, a friend of mine, Jay, who was a writer that I knew, uh, who was, um, getting married to a friend of mine.
所以我，嗯，我有个朋友杰伊，他是我认识的一位作家，他当时正要和我的一位朋友结婚。

00:13:04.392 --> 00:13:05.140
He was great.
他很棒。

00:13:05.140 --> 00:13:06.118
He's a great guy.
他是个很棒的人。

00:13:06.118 --> 00:13:07.441
He remains a great guy.
他现在依然是个很棒的人。

00:13:07.441 --> 00:13:14.919
And he told me that he and his wife had gone down to Mexico and they had done something called ayahuasca, which I had never heard.
他告诉我，他和妻子去了一趟墨西哥，做了一件叫“死藤水”（ayahuasca）的事情，我以前从未听说过。

00:13:14.919 --> 00:13:16.356
I'd never heard the word.
我从未听过这个词。

00:13:16.356 --> 00:13:17.389
Hey, this is Josh.
嘿，我是乔什。

00:13:17.389 --> 00:13:34.794
I'm interrupting my own story for a public service announcement, which is to say, uh, I'm about to talk, uh, very lovingly and at great length about ayahuasca, which is this indigenous plant medicine that I worked with quite a bit, but starting in between seasons two and three of how I met your mother.
我打断自己的故事是为了做一个公益声明，也就是说，我接下来要非常深情且详尽地谈论死藤水，这是一种我使用过多次的本土植物药，始于《老爸老妈浪漫史》第二季和第三季之间。

00:13:34.794 --> 00:13:44.846
And when we finished the discussion, I realized I should put a little disclaimer around this or a little bit of brackets, which is to say, this is a very powerful psychedelic.
当我们结束讨论时，我意识到我应该对此加个免责声明或括号说明，也就是说，这是一种非常强大的迷幻剂。

00:13:44.846 --> 00:13:46.742
It is not to be taken recklessly.
绝不能鲁莽使用。

00:13:46.742 --> 00:13:50.935
If you're going to do it, find a shaman, find a ceremonial kind of group.
如果你打算尝试，请找一位萨满，找一个仪式性的团体。

00:13:50.935 --> 00:13:52.371
It's a very sacred thing.
这是一件非常神圣的事情。

00:13:52.371 --> 00:13:58.920
And if you take it in a casual manner with people you don't know or don't trust, you can get into a world of hurt.
如果你在不了解或不信任的人面前随意使用，你可能会陷入巨大的痛苦之中。

00:13:58.919 --> 00:14:08.039
So I just wanted to put some brackets around this before we go on and talk about this, just so it doesn't seem like I'm promoting this recklessly, because it's quite a big deal.
所以我只是想在继续谈论之前加上这些括号，这样看起来就不会像我在鲁莽地推广它，因为这确实是一件大事。

00:14:08.039 --> 00:14:09.665
And I just wanted to say that.
我只是想说这些。

00:14:09.665 --> 00:14:11.399
All right, back to me and Craig.
好了，回到我和克雷格的话题。

00:14:12.120 --> 00:14:19.502
But I remember when he said that word, ayahuasca, something in my chest kind of went, like I felt a little like, what is that?
但我记得当他说出那个词“死藤水”时，我的胸口有一种感觉，就像我感到有点……那是什么？

00:14:19.502 --> 00:14:23.076
Like it really was a word that had a kind of frequency to it.
它确实是一个带有一种频率的词。

00:14:23.076 --> 00:14:24.306
It called me forward.
它在召唤我。

00:14:24.306 --> 00:14:31.747
And then this friend of mine, Catherine sent me an email and she said, my friend David has been down in Brazil with this group.
然后我的朋友凯瑟琳给我发了一封邮件，她说，我的朋友大卫在巴西和这个团体在一起。

00:14:31.747 --> 00:14:37.371
And this man Ralph takes people down there and they work with a shaman and they drink ayahuasca.
这个叫拉尔夫的人带人们去那里，他们和萨满一起工作，喝死藤水。

00:14:37.371 --> 00:14:40.360
This was not long after I had first heard the word.
这离我第一次听到这个词没过多久。

00:14:40.360 --> 00:14:42.849
And I tend to take that stuff seriously.
我倾向于认真对待这些事情。

00:14:42.849 --> 00:14:50.879
If you start hearing a word or a person or a movie, that keeps, it's like maybe it's meant for you, you know, I believe that too.
如果你不断听到一个词、一个人或一部电影，也许它是命中注定的，你知道，我也相信这一点。

00:14:50.879 --> 00:15:01.585
So I was seeing a woman that I had met through my meditation community, and I took her to hear an intro talk by this guy, Ralph Miller, who was coming to LA.
当时我正在和一个通过冥想社区认识的女性约会，我带她去听了这个叫拉尔夫·米勒的人的介绍讲座，他当时正要来洛杉矶。

00:15:01.585 --> 00:15:05.539
Ralph remains, this guy remains one of my dearest friends.
拉尔夫至今仍是我最亲爱的朋友之一。

00:15:05.539 --> 00:15:07.517
He's an incredible character.
他是个不可思议的人物。

00:15:07.517 --> 00:15:19.313
He's kind of like, if the dude from the big Lebowski just like if you got to hang out with him at 71, like he's got this really low voice and he just, he's never in a hurry.
他有点像……如果《谋杀绿脚趾》里的那个家伙，如果你在71岁时和他一起闲逛，他声音很低沉，而且从不着急。

00:15:19.313 --> 00:15:29.200
You know, I would say like if everyone marches to the beat or their own drummer, his is just like a solid like kick drum, just like a really low.
你知道，我会说如果每个人都按照自己的节奏行事，他的节奏就像一个稳健的底鼓，非常低沉。

00:15:29.200 --> 00:15:33.946
Yeah, it's just like he's just, he's an incredible character.
是的，他就是这样，他是个不可思议的人物。

00:15:33.946 --> 00:15:35.580
He was at my wedding.
他参加了我的婚礼。

00:15:35.580 --> 00:15:50.519
And I met this This guy in December of 2006, I want to say it was, and he, he just started talking about the, he used to be a travel agent and now he's like a kind of psychedelic travel agent.
我在2006年12月认识了他，我想是这样，他开始谈论……他以前是个旅行社代理人，现在他就像是一个迷幻旅行代理人。

00:15:50.519 --> 00:15:56.799
He would take people down to Brazil to buy E on the northeast coast in a little town called Bar and Grande.
他会带人去巴西东北海岸的一个叫巴拉格兰德的小镇。

00:15:56.799 --> 00:16:06.259
And I sat there and I listened to, I really liked meeting him, I just, he was one of those people I just immediately trusted for whatever reason, which was good because you want to trust whoever you're doing this kind of thing with.
我坐在那里听着，我真的很喜欢见到他，他就是那种我无论出于什么原因都会立即信任的人，这很好，因为你想要信任和你一起做这种事的人。

00:16:06.259 --> 00:16:07.259
I wouldn't imagine that's a few.
我无法想象那是少数。

00:16:07.259 --> 00:16:13.139
Within five minutes of his presentation, I was like, I'm going down to South America, I'm going to do this.
在他演讲的五分钟内，我就想，我要去南美，我要做这件事。

00:16:13.139 --> 00:16:30.350
And I remember, and by the way, let me just tell you, for those of you who don't know, and I've talked about this a lot in various interviews and I've written about it, but ayahuasca is an indigenous plant medicine, which is, it's a combination of a vine and a bush that grow in the Amazon.
我记得，顺便说一句，让我告诉你们，对于那些不知道的人，我在各种采访中谈过很多次，也写过关于它的文章，死藤水是一种本土植物药，它是生长在亚马逊雨林中的一种藤蔓和一种灌木的结合体。

00:16:30.350 --> 00:16:41.429
And something about the pharmacology of these two, when they're brewed together, this vine and this bush, you drink it and it's this sludgy, very disgusting mixture.
当这两种植物被一起熬制时，它们的药理作用很奇特，你喝下它，那是一种粘稠、非常恶心的混合物。

00:16:42.470 --> 00:16:56.350
And when you drink it, the effect it has on your body is it puts you into this incredibly strange visionary space that is like nothing I'd ever experienced.
当你喝下它时，它对你身体的影响是让你进入一个极其奇怪的幻觉空间，那是我从未经历过的。

00:16:56.350 --> 00:17:05.910
It can be very rigorous, there can be vomiting and other things that are, that sounds horrific, but it's not like vomiting from like too much drinking or the stomach flu.
它可能非常严苛，可能会有呕吐和其他反应，听起来很可怕，但这不像喝多了或肠胃感冒引起的呕吐。

00:17:05.910 --> 00:17:09.390
It's like the way I had a Columbian shaman describe it to me.
就像一位哥伦比亚萨满向我描述的那样。

00:17:09.390 --> 00:17:12.549
He said, well, it's like sweating, if you don't want to be sweating, it's uncomfortable.
他说，嗯，这就像出汗，如果你不想出汗，那会很不舒服。

00:17:12.549 --> 00:17:14.789
But if you're sweating because you're exercising, you like it.
但如果你是因为锻炼而出汗，你就会喜欢它。

00:17:14.789 --> 00:17:22.390
So it's a little more like, you get out things that are like, oh, this is not something I want in my body.
所以它更像是，你排出了那些“哦，这不是我想留在体内的东西”。

00:17:22.390 --> 00:17:25.910
And there's a kind of, this sounds so weird when I talk about it.
而且有一种……当我谈论它时，这听起来太奇怪了。

00:17:25.910 --> 00:17:29.029
And I used to be so, I used to struggle and struggle and struggle how to talk about this.
我曾经非常、非常、非常努力地想知道该如何谈论这件事。

00:17:29.029 --> 00:17:32.812
But there's a kind of guiding spirit you that guides you.
但有一种引导你的精神力量。

00:17:32.812 --> 00:17:34.338
This was my experience.
这就是我的经历。

00:17:34.338 --> 00:17:35.533
It works with you.
它与你共同作用。

00:17:35.533 --> 00:17:36.528
It teaches you.
它会教导你。

00:17:36.528 --> 00:17:38.187
It teaches through image.
它通过意象来教导。

00:17:38.187 --> 00:17:39.912
It teaches through memory.
它通过记忆来教导。

00:17:39.912 --> 00:17:42.301
It teaches sometimes it says things.
它有时会通过言语来教导。

00:17:42.301 --> 00:17:45.221
But it's got this kind of course curriculum.
但它有一套类似于课程的体系。

00:17:45.221 --> 00:17:51.923
And I, the ceremonies that I did were with a Colombian shaman named Bernay, who was really wonderful.
我参加的仪式是由一位名叫伯纳的哥伦比亚萨满主持的，他真的很棒。

00:17:51.923 --> 00:17:55.175
But I went down to Brazil for almost three weeks.
但我去了巴西待了近三周。

00:17:55.175 --> 00:17:57.166
I did six of these ceremonies.
我参加了六场这样的仪式。

00:17:57.166 --> 00:18:11.234
And I just after the first one, I remember talking to Ralph as this, you know, the sun was coming up and looking out at the ocean and just feeling like my life is different, like something is different right now.
我记得在第一场仪式结束后，当太阳升起时，我看着大海，和拉尔夫交谈，感觉我的生活变得不同了，好像现在有什么东西改变了。

00:18:11.234 --> 00:18:24.505
And I, you know, that first night, I felt I hadn't experience of unconditional love, maybe for the first time in my life, like, it felt like unconditional love had saturated every molecule of my body.
那天晚上，我体验到了无条件的爱，这可能是我一生中第一次，感觉无条件的爱渗透了我身体的每一个分子。

00:18:24.505 --> 00:18:31.539
Like there was, there was no part of of my body or being that was untouched by this pervasive cosmic love.
就好像我身体或存在的每一个部分，都感受到了这种无处不在的宇宙之爱。

00:18:31.539 --> 00:18:34.900
And it was so beautiful and so healing.
那感觉太美妙、太治愈了。

00:18:34.900 --> 00:18:47.579
And I remember because the spirit of ayahuasca, as they say, is like incredibly feminine, not for everyone, but for me, it was just this feminine presence that was loving me.
我记得因为人们常说死藤水的精神是非常女性化的，虽然并非对每个人都如此，但对我来说，那是一种充满爱意的女性存在。

00:18:47.579 --> 00:18:49.740
And they call her the mother or the grandmother.
他们称她为母亲或祖母。

00:18:49.740 --> 00:18:54.619
And I remember lying on the beach in Brazil, staring up at the night sky.
我记得躺在巴西的海滩上，凝视着夜空。

00:18:54.619 --> 00:19:04.539
I had a dim memory of that I was on a TV show on CBS, like the smallest memory that was also part of my life, but I remember going, oh.
我当时对自己在CBS拍电视剧这件事只有一点模糊的记忆，那只是我生活的一小部分，但我记得当时想，哦。

00:19:04.539 --> 00:19:07.339
That must have been a great feeling at that moment for that to be that small.
那一刻，能把那件事看得那么轻，感觉一定很棒。

00:19:07.339 --> 00:19:09.980
That's the thing that was so dominant in your head space.
那是你脑海中占据主导地位的事情。

00:19:09.980 --> 00:19:10.819
Yes, yes.
是的，是的。

00:19:10.819 --> 00:19:18.500
It suddenly felt like I stepped into something so much cosmically bigger, but I remember saying, how I met your mother?
突然感觉我进入了一个在宇宙层面上大得多的境界，但我记得我说，老爸老妈浪漫史？

00:19:18.500 --> 00:19:22.180
Like this is the mother, this is not the brand mother.
就像这是母亲，这不是那个剧里的母亲。

00:19:22.180 --> 00:19:30.980
No matter how I met, the mother was, I was on a TV show called How I Make a Mother, and I was freaked out by fame, and I came down to South America, and I drank this brew, and then, you know, that's really funny.
不管我怎么遇见，母亲就是母亲，我当时在拍一部叫《老爸老妈浪漫史》的电视剧，我被名气吓坏了，我来到南美，喝了这种药水，然后，你知道，这真的很有趣。

00:19:30.980 --> 00:19:32.579
I've never heard you tell that before.
我以前从没听你讲过这个。

00:19:32.579 --> 00:19:34.099
That's kind of a fitting way to say it.
这真是一个贴切的说法。

00:19:34.099 --> 00:19:35.339
So I did these six ceremonies.
所以我做了这六场仪式。

00:19:35.339 --> 00:19:47.900
I came back and I felt like the whites in my eyes were just, you know, glistening, and I felt kind of newly born, and then it started to erode, and it started to erode because I started drinking alcohol again.
我回来时感觉眼白都在闪闪发光，感觉像是重获新生，但后来这种感觉开始消退，因为我又开始喝酒了。

00:19:47.900 --> 00:19:51.109
I didn't drink when I was there.
我在那里的时候没喝酒。

00:19:51.109 --> 00:19:53.990
And I think I mentioned this, but I got punched in the face that summer.
我想我提到过，那个夏天我被人打了一拳。

00:19:53.990 --> 00:19:55.349
Like, yeah.
是啊。

00:19:55.349 --> 00:19:56.950
Wait, okay, pause.
等等，好吧，暂停。

00:19:56.950 --> 00:19:57.789
When were you?
你当时在哪？

00:19:57.789 --> 00:19:59.950
What month would you have been in Brazil?
你是在几月份去的巴西？

00:19:59.950 --> 00:20:01.750
So I didn't go to the cast party.
我没去杀青派对。

00:20:01.750 --> 00:20:02.589
I remember that.
我记得那个。

00:20:02.589 --> 00:20:04.150
I left the following morning.
我第二天早上就走了。

00:20:04.150 --> 00:20:06.269
Like we wrapped and I left for Brazil the next day.
我们拍完戏，第二天我就去了巴西。

00:20:06.269 --> 00:20:07.190
You went right away.
你马上就去了。

00:20:07.190 --> 00:20:08.029
I went right away.
我马上就去了。

00:20:08.029 --> 00:20:11.109
I missed the wrap party of season two.
我错过了第二季的杀青派对。

00:20:11.109 --> 00:20:12.430
I went to Brazil.
我去了巴西。

00:20:12.430 --> 00:20:14.069
So something like March or April.
所以大概是三月或四月。

00:20:14.069 --> 00:20:14.910
Yeah, it was March.
是的，是三月。

00:20:14.910 --> 00:20:16.630
It was March into April.
是从三月到四月。

00:20:16.630 --> 00:20:18.910
Yeah, I would say, yeah.
是的，我会说是的。

00:20:18.910 --> 00:20:37.150
And then I had this like drunken night in Columbus, Ohio when I was visiting my parents where I just drank too much and I was trying to, I was out with this woman who I think I don't know if she told me she had a boyfriend but she reminded me she had a boyfriend but I kind of didn't care.
后来在俄亥俄州哥伦布市探望父母时，我喝醉了一晚，喝得太多了，当时我和一个女人在一起，我不确定她是否告诉过我她有男朋友，但她提醒过我她有男朋友，但我当时不太在意。

00:20:37.150 --> 00:20:42.789
And then her boyfriend like kind of jumped me in the parking lot after at the end of the night.
然后那天晚上结束时，她男朋友在停车场袭击了我。

00:20:42.789 --> 00:20:47.950
And he punched me in the face twice and I really was kind of dinged up by this.
他朝我脸上打了两拳，我确实因此受了点伤。

00:20:48.910 --> 00:20:52.995
And then I had- Did you know the boyfriend or was like- No, no, no.
然后我——你认识那个男朋友吗，还是说——不，不，不。

00:20:52.995 --> 00:20:53.910
That's the boy.
那是那个男孩。

00:20:53.910 --> 00:20:55.910
That was how you met the boyfriend.
那就是你遇见那个男朋友的方式。

00:20:55.910 --> 00:20:56.910
No, not true.
不，不是真的。

00:20:56.910 --> 00:21:03.910
We were at another place drinking and he came to our table and tried to get her to leave with him and she wouldn't.
我们在另一个地方喝酒，他来到我们的桌子旁，试图让她跟他走，但她没走。

00:21:03.910 --> 00:21:04.910
Oh, wow.
哦，哇。

00:21:04.910 --> 00:21:06.910
Which was probably- This was a crazy night, yeah.
这可能是——那真是一个疯狂的夜晚，是的。

00:21:06.910 --> 00:21:07.910
It was crazy.
太疯狂了。

00:21:07.910 --> 00:21:08.910
Yeah.
是的。

00:21:08.910 --> 00:21:18.359
So then Ralph was leading another trip to Columbia that I could go on before having to be back for production.
后来拉尔夫又组织了一次去哥伦比亚的旅行，我可以在回剧组拍戏前参加。

00:21:18.359 --> 00:21:19.112
production.
拍戏。

00:21:19.112 --> 00:21:22.671
So I went down to Armenia in the jungle of Columbia.
所以我去了哥伦比亚丛林里的亚美尼亚。

00:21:22.671 --> 00:21:24.040
We flew into Bogota.
我们飞到了波哥大。

00:21:24.039 --> 00:21:28.440
I went to this place in the rainforest and called Armenia this beautiful property.
我去了雨林里一个叫亚美尼亚的地方，那里有一处美丽的房产。

00:21:28.440 --> 00:21:32.502
And I did three more ceremonies with the same show.
我和同一个萨满又做了三场仪式。

00:21:32.502 --> 00:21:33.617
In the summer.
在夏天。

00:21:33.617 --> 00:21:34.732
In the summer.
在夏天。

00:21:34.732 --> 00:21:36.484
Yeah, this was August.
是的，那是八月。

00:21:36.484 --> 00:21:37.360
Yeah, okay.
好的。

00:21:37.360 --> 00:21:46.998
And then on my eighth ceremony, so the second ceremony of that set, I had an evening that was entirely about my drinking.
在我的第八场仪式，也就是那组仪式的第二场，我经历了一个完全关于我酗酒的夜晚。

00:21:46.998 --> 00:21:50.662
It was like, that was almost the entire night.
那几乎是整晚的主题。

00:21:50.662 --> 00:21:54.963
And I realized that I got punched because I was drunk.
我意识到我被打是因为我喝醉了。

00:21:54.963 --> 00:21:58.468
And I also had bought a house at that point.
那时我还买了一栋房子。

00:21:58.468 --> 00:22:01.176
And I had a barbecue at the house.
我在家里办了烧烤派对。

00:22:01.176 --> 00:22:05.000
I remember Neil and David came to this barbecue.
我记得尼尔和大卫都来了。

00:22:05.000 --> 00:22:14.319
And I, my friend Rachel and I, who ended up getting sober actually, she came with me to like a Bevmo or something, and we bought so much liquor.
我和我的朋友瑞秋，她后来也戒酒了，她和我一起去了一家酒类商店，我们买了很多酒。

00:22:14.319 --> 00:22:20.119
Like we bought liquor for four times the amount of people that were gonna be at this party.
我们买的酒量是参加派对人数的四倍。

00:22:20.119 --> 00:22:25.920
And so I had a vision of this house that I was about to move into, and the only thing that was there was liquor.
我看到了一个关于我即将搬进去的房子的幻象，里面唯一的东西就是酒。

00:22:25.920 --> 00:22:26.759
Wow.
哇。

00:22:26.759 --> 00:22:31.759
It was just like bottles and warm beers and bottles of booze.
到处都是瓶子、温啤酒和烈酒。

00:22:32.799 --> 00:22:44.009
And then I had this vision of myself on the couch, kind of sinking into the couch as I drank more and more, you know, I could feel myself melt into the couch.
然后我看到了自己坐在沙发上的幻象，随着我喝得越来越多，我感觉自己陷进了沙发里，你知道，我能感觉到自己融化在沙发里。

00:22:44.009 --> 00:22:53.609
And then I felt myself lift off the couch and like go into the astral realm, like the heavenly spheres.
然后我感觉到自己从沙发上飘了起来，进入了星界，就像天堂的领域。

00:22:53.609 --> 00:22:56.450
And I could see my house in Los Angeles down below.
我能看到下方洛杉矶的房子。

00:22:56.450 --> 00:23:03.369
And I was almost like freed from the kind of the God of alcohol or the demon of alcohol.
我几乎从酒精之神或酒精恶魔中解脱了出来。

00:23:03.369 --> 00:23:05.769
Like I was set free, you know.
我获得了自由，你知道。

00:23:05.769 --> 00:23:08.690
And so after the ceremony, I was very thrown.
仪式结束后，我感到非常震撼。

00:23:08.690 --> 00:23:13.690
And it was very clear that there was an invitation at least to stop drinking alcohol.
很明显，这至少是一个停止饮酒的邀请。

00:23:13.690 --> 00:23:18.089
And in the airport, I called my friend Dion, who's one of my dearest friends.
在机场，我给我的朋友迪翁打了电话，他是我最亲密的朋友之一。

00:23:18.089 --> 00:23:22.410
He's now a writer on the Tonight Show.
他现在是《今夜秀》的编剧。

00:23:22.410 --> 00:23:27.329
And he got sober in between our first and second, at some point in our first year at grad school.
他在我们研究生一年级的某个时候戒了酒。

00:23:27.329 --> 00:23:29.490
So he'd been already sober a long time.
所以他已经戒酒很久了。

00:23:29.490 --> 00:23:32.009
And I told him, I said, I think I need to quit drinking.
我告诉他，我说，我想我需要戒酒。

00:23:32.009 --> 00:23:36.329
I remember talking to him in the Miami airport, and I started crying when I said it because it was so...
我记得在迈阿密机场和他通话，说出这句话时我哭了，因为这太……

00:23:36.329 --> 00:23:37.329
Yeah.
是的。

00:23:37.329 --> 00:23:39.490
It just felt like, I don't know if I have this in.
感觉就像，我不知道我是否能做到。

00:23:39.490 --> 00:23:44.730
Like, it was like, I was saying something I didn't want to actually follow through on, but I knew I needed to say it.
就像我在说一件我并不想真正执行的事情，但我知道我必须说出来。

00:23:44.730 --> 00:23:45.650
Yeah, yeah.
是的，是的。

00:23:45.650 --> 00:23:54.640
And I remember him saying, nature hates a vacuum, you know, that all that energy and space that was taken up by your drinking, something else is going to come fill it.
我记得他说，自然界厌恶真空，你知道，你喝酒所占据的所有能量和空间，会有别的东西来填补。

00:23:54.640 --> 00:23:55.480
Right.
对。

00:23:55.480 --> 00:23:57.119
And it'll be interesting to see what he said.
看看他说的会发生什么，这很有趣。

00:23:57.119 --> 00:23:58.920
I want to see what happens, you know.
我想看看会发生什么，你知道。

00:23:58.920 --> 00:24:01.799
So I remember coming back, it's a very supportive comment.
所以我记得回来后，这是一个非常有支持性的评论。

00:24:01.799 --> 00:24:03.119
That's a very wise comment.
那是一个非常有智慧的评论。

00:24:03.119 --> 00:24:06.480
Yeah, I like, it's a very smart way to put it.
是啊，我觉得，这种说法非常精辟。

00:24:06.480 --> 00:24:07.319
I bet that helps.
我敢说那肯定有帮助。

00:24:07.319 --> 00:24:08.160
Yeah.
是啊。

00:24:08.160 --> 00:24:09.000
Yeah.
是啊。

00:24:09.000 --> 00:24:12.000
Oh, he's helped me out of a lot of jams over the years.
噢，这些年来他帮我摆脱过很多困境。

00:24:12.000 --> 00:24:12.839
Yeah.
是啊。

00:24:13.940 --> 00:24:19.700
And then I remember coming back, it might have been, when did Tina and Dave get married?
然后我记得回来的时候，那可能是，蒂娜和戴夫是什么时候结婚的？

00:24:19.700 --> 00:24:21.500
Was that at the beginning of third season?
那是第三季开始的时候吗？

00:24:21.500 --> 00:24:22.420
I forget.
我忘了。

00:24:22.420 --> 00:24:25.259
There was a wedding, there was like a how I met your mother wedding.
当时有一场婚礼，就像《老爸老妈浪漫史》里的婚礼一样。

00:24:25.259 --> 00:24:26.259
That sounds right.
听起来没错。

00:24:26.259 --> 00:24:27.099
That sounds right.
听起来没错。

00:24:27.099 --> 00:24:28.099
And we were all at the wedding.
我们当时都在婚礼上。

00:24:28.099 --> 00:24:30.019
And we'd props and...
我们还有道具和……

00:24:30.019 --> 00:24:30.859
Props and hair.
道具组和发型组。

00:24:30.859 --> 00:24:31.700
Props and hair.
道具组和发型组。

00:24:31.700 --> 00:24:32.539
Props and hair got married.
道具组和发型组结婚了。

00:24:32.539 --> 00:24:33.900
And him and couple props and hair.
还有他和几个道具组和发型组的人。

00:24:33.900 --> 00:24:45.089
But we were all at the cast, and we were all at a table and it was my first kind of big party and I wasn't drinking and I remember Seagull looks over at me and he goes, you look really happy, you look really good.
但我们演员都在，我们都坐在桌子旁，那是我第一次参加那种大型派对，我当时没喝酒，我记得西格尔看着我说，你看上去真的很开心，你看上去状态很好。

00:24:46.289 --> 00:25:00.467
And it was interesting because Seagull and I were like, the first two seasons like, we were drinking buddies, you know, we like, we hit the town together and but I remember him noting that it looked kind of good on me and I didn't drink for four years.
这很有趣，因为西格尔和我，在前两季的时候，我们是酒友，你知道，我们一起出去玩，但我记得他注意到这种状态对我来说很好，我后来四年没喝酒。

00:25:00.467 --> 00:25:03.168
I continued to do do ayahuasca in various forms.
我继续以各种形式服用死藤水。

00:25:03.168 --> 00:25:05.249
I found, you know, other communities.
我找到了，你知道，其他的社群。

00:25:05.249 --> 00:25:07.106
And I ended up doing a lot of it.
最后我做了很多次。

00:25:07.106 --> 00:25:09.019
And I didn't drink for four years.
而且我四年没喝酒。

00:25:09.019 --> 00:25:12.169
And then I, I kind of tried to drink, didn't go so well.
后来我，我试着喝了一点，结果不太好。

00:25:12.169 --> 00:25:18.302
By the end of how I met your mother, I remember the ninth season, I was, I was back to drinking a little bit.
到《老爸老妈浪漫史》结束时，我记得第九季的时候，我，我又开始喝一点酒了。

00:25:18.302 --> 00:25:22.409
You and I had a couple old fashions, I remember, like post post shooting.
我记得你和我喝过几杯古典鸡尾酒，就在拍摄结束后。

00:25:22.409 --> 00:25:26.234
And then, I think it was 2017 or 18 was the last time I had a drink.
然后，我想2017年或18年是我最后一次喝酒。

00:25:26.234 --> 00:25:32.930
But And I would say, since I was 32 years old, I'm 51 right now, I've spent a lot more time not drinking than drinking.
但是，我想说，从我32岁开始，我现在51岁了，我花在不喝酒上的时间比喝酒的时间多得多。

00:25:32.930 --> 00:25:35.809
It's been about eight years, seven, eight years since I've had a drink.
我已经有大约八年，七、八年没喝过酒了。

00:25:35.809 --> 00:25:43.289
And I'm really, I'm a happy non-drinker, you know, like, I'm not, I'm what you call California sober.
而且我真的，我是一个快乐的戒酒者，你知道，就像，我属于那种所谓的“加州清醒”。

00:25:43.289 --> 00:25:44.289
I alter my consciousness in other ways.
我会用其他方式改变我的意识。

00:25:44.289 --> 00:25:54.009
I'm not like a, like a stone cold sober person, but, um, you know, there was, on my mom's side, there's, there's alcoholism and not from her, but, uh, you know, her father.
我不是那种，那种滴酒不沾的人，但是，嗯，你知道，在我母亲那边，有，有酗酒史，不是她，而是，嗯，你知道，她父亲。

00:25:54.009 --> 00:26:04.410
And I just felt like I could feel when I did the ayahuasca that it was like in me, you know, like that feeling of like insatiability, like I can't moderate this.
我只是觉得，当我服用死藤水时，我能感觉到它就在我体内，你知道，那种无法满足的感觉，就像我无法控制这种欲望。

00:26:04.410 --> 00:26:08.650
And once I tried to drink like a gentleman and realized like I kind of couldn't, I stopped.
一旦我试着像个绅士一样喝酒，却发现我根本做不到，我就停了。

00:26:08.650 --> 00:26:12.410
And it's been like a really good decision in my life.
这对我的人生来说是一个非常好的决定。

00:26:12.410 --> 00:26:13.730
And I credit ayahuasca with that.
我把这归功于死藤水。

00:26:13.730 --> 00:26:19.089
So I came back to how I met your mother having done nine ayahuasca ceremonies, stop drinking.
所以我带着九次死藤水仪式的经历回到了《老爸老妈浪漫史》，并停止了饮酒。

00:26:19.089 --> 00:26:29.130
When I told you when I saw, when I see the end of season two in the beginning of season three, I always think, there's a real before and after here for me personally.
当我告诉你，当我看到第二季结尾和第三季开头时，我总是想，对我个人而言，这里有一个真正的分水岭。

00:26:29.130 --> 00:26:34.930
And I could feel, I always felt like my beginning work on season three, I'm very proud of.
我能感觉到，我一直觉得我对第三季的早期工作感到非常自豪。

00:26:34.930 --> 00:26:47.250
I felt really in the pocket, I felt really dropped in, I felt really present, I felt really much more okay with being the lead of a big, you know, a big show.
我感觉自己完全进入了状态，我感觉自己完全沉浸其中，我感觉自己非常在场，我感觉自己更能接受作为一部大制作剧集的主演。

00:26:47.250 --> 00:26:48.177
I really saw it.
我真的看到了。

00:26:48.177 --> 00:26:51.423
This rewatch, I really saw that shift in a way I didn't.
这次重温，我真的看到了那种转变，一种我当时没意识到的转变。

00:26:51.423 --> 00:26:55.885
I guess at the time, I kind of knew, but I really see it now when I watch it.
我想当时我多少知道一点，但现在看的时候我真的看出来了。

00:26:55.885 --> 00:26:58.609
So it is sort of good doing this in the middle.
所以现在回过头来做这件事确实挺好的。

00:26:58.609 --> 00:27:10.157
Well, I think I got to step into something that felt so much bigger than Hollywood, so much bigger than anything that I had ever encountered before.
嗯，我想我得以踏入一个感觉比好莱坞大得多，比我之前遇到过的任何事情都大得多的领域。

00:27:10.157 --> 00:27:17.180
It felt, you know, I keep using the word cosmic, but it's the only word that's big enough.
它感觉，你知道，我一直用“宇宙”这个词，但这是唯一足够大的词。

00:27:17.180 --> 00:27:29.220
If people have done psychedelics, but especially ayahuasca, which I think is one of the more powerful and beautiful ones, it's very hard to put in words, and it's a little bit.
如果人们尝试过迷幻剂，尤其是死藤水，我认为它是其中更强大、更美妙的一种，它很难用语言表达，而且有一点……

00:27:29.220 --> 00:27:36.700
I read someone who said, if you want to take it seriously, you have to take it, you can't kind of intellectualize your way into it.
我读过某人的话，他说，如果你想认真对待它，你就必须去体验它，你不能靠理智去理解它。

00:27:36.700 --> 00:27:40.442
But I did, after the morning, after my first ceremony, I started writing, and I wrote a book.
但我确实做了，在第一次仪式后的第二天早上，我开始写作，我写了一本书。

00:27:40.442 --> 00:27:43.057
